## About the exhibition

The Brightwater Maritime Museum is pleased to present *Tides of Trade*, an exhibition that follows the spice, tea and cotton routes between 1600 and 1850.

Through original ship ledgers, navigation instruments and a full-size reconstruction of a cargo hold, visitors can trace how these goods moved across the oceans over two and a half centuries.

The centerpiece is the **1783 log of the brig *Hesper***, shown publicly for the first time.

